From: Abdelhafid DJIDEL <266947999+hafid-logic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 22:35:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests(devices): pin IsolatedNetwork receive buffer, empty,
 and closed boundaries

### What
Pins `IsolatedNetwork::receive`: an empty queue returns `QueueEmpty`, a buffer smaller than the queued frame returns `InvalidPayload` without consuming it, an exact-fit buffer receives the frame, and a closed network returns `Closed`.

### Why it matters
The receive path guards buffer sizing and queue state. The existing suite sends and receives exact-fit frames but never exercises the small-buffer, empty-queue, or closed paths, so removing those guards survives it.

### Mutation evidence (fail-then-pass)
| Mutant | Existing suite | New test |
|---|---|---|
| remove `output.len() < frame.len` guard | PASS (survives) | FAIL (killed) |
| remove `self.len == 0` guard | PASS (survives) | FAIL (killed) |

Baseline (clean tree + new test): PASS. Reproduce: `cargo test -p ginux-devices --lib receive_rejects`.

Prepared with AI assistance; reviewed by me.
---
 crates/ginux-devices/src/lib.rs | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 pipe==1===                      |  1 +
 2 files changed, 20 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 pipe==1===

diff --git a/crates/ginux-devices/src/lib.rs b/crates/ginux-devices/src/lib.rs
index 592c0f15..63189346 100644
--- a/crates/ginux-devices/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/ginux-devices/src/lib.rs
@@ -793,4 +793,23 @@ mod tests {
         assert_eq!(out[0].kind, DeviceKind::Zero);
         assert_eq!(registry.views(99, &mut out), 0);
     }
+
+    #[test]
+    fn receive_rejects_small_buffer_and_reports_closed_and_empty() {
+        let mut net: IsolatedNetwork<2> = IsolatedNetwork::new();
+        // empty queue
+        assert_eq!(net.receive(&mut [0; 8]), Err(DeviceError::QueueEmpty));
+        net.send(b"hello").unwrap();
+        // buffer too small for the queued frame
+        assert_eq!(net.receive(&mut [0; 4]), Err(DeviceError::InvalidPayload));
+        // exact-fit buffer succeeds
+        let mut buf = [0; 5];
+        assert_eq!(net.receive(&mut buf), Ok(5));
+        assert_eq!(&buf, b"hello");
+        // now empty again
+        assert_eq!(net.receive(&mut [0; 8]), Err(DeviceError::QueueEmpty));
+        // closed network rejects receive
+        net.close();
+        assert_eq!(net.receive(&mut [0; 8]), Err(DeviceError::Closed));
+    }
 }
diff --git a/pipe==1=== b/pipe==1===
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..ad71bfcb
--- /dev/null
+++ b/pipe==1===
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
